Add a --json flag to this CLI. With --json it should print one JSON object per file with keys file, lines, words instead of the text line. Keep the default behaviour unchanged. Here is cli.py:

```python
import argparse, sys, pathlib

def count(path: pathlib.Path) -> tuple[int, int]:
    text = path.read_text()
    return len(text.splitlines()), len(text.split())

def main(argv=None):
    p = argparse.ArgumentParser(description="Count lines and words.")
    p.add_argument("files", nargs="+", type=pathlib.Path)
    args = p.parse_args(argv)
    for f in args.files:
        lines, words = count(f)
        print(f"{f}: {lines} lines, {words} words")

if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main())
```

